{
 "id": "gap_verify",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "time_axis"
 ],
 "description": "THE ABDUCED INTERMEDIATES, CHECKED -- the constraint the gapabduce rung (97000-97999) named as the lever it earned. Its deepest measured result was a negative: THE OPERATOR HAS NO DISCRIMINATIVE POWER, accepting independent random endpoints at ~1/steps because any two same-shape figures ARE rigid translates. Its intermediates were emitted and CHECKED AGAINST NOTHING. This seed checks them: in a scene with other content, G^t(f_before) makes a falsifiable prediction at every gap tick, and STRICT ACCOUNTABILITY (every predicted cell must coincide with an observed cell, exact integer coordinates) makes interpolation REFUSABLE. Flag-gated on agent.gap_verify_enabled==1, OFF by default (PROTOCOL 9); inert without it AND matches only status=='gap_vseq'.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "gap_verify",
  "description": "an interpolation that can be WRONG. The abduction fits two endpoints and one free generator, which always fit; the intermediates it implies do not. Continuation is constrained because verification across every consecutive pair can fail -- this gives interpolation the same kind of constraint, against the scene rather than against a third sample."
 },
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
